{"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent"]]},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Traffluent"}],"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Privacy Manifests","role":"article"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/traffluent\/privacymanifests"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What each module can collect, the required-reason APIs it calls, and the privacy manifest it ships, so you can fill in your app’s own manifest and privacy labels."}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PrivacyManifests"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Traffluent collects nothing on its own. It records only the events your app tracks and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"context your app turns on: every kind of automatic instrumentation and every standard enricher is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"opt in. It sends records only to the destinations your app gives a delivery, to endpoints your app"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"names. None of it is used for tracking as Apple defines it: no module links what it records with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other companies’ data, reads the advertising identifier, fingerprints the device, or works around"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the user’s consent or App Tracking Transparency. Every manifest declares "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPrivacyTracking"},{"type":"text","text":" as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"},{"type":"text","text":" and lists no tracking domains."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each module that can produce data of one of Apple’s collected data types ships a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy"},{"text":" declaring it. SwiftPM and Bazel both put it in a resource bundle named","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Traffluent_<Module>.bundle"},{"text":", which Xcode and rules_apple copy into your app, where Xcode’s privacy","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"report finds it. A module your app doesn’t link adds nothing to the report.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Required-reason APIs","anchor":"Required-reason-APIs","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No Traffluent module calls an API on Apple’s list of required-reason APIs, so every manifest’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is empty. The list’s categories are file timestamps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), system boot time"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategorySystemBootTime","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), disk space"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryDiskSpace","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), active keyboards"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryActiveKeyboards","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") and user defaults"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"). The modules that come nearest:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Module","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"What it calls"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Why none is a required-reason API"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence","type":"reference"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"swift-system’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FileDescriptor"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"open"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"read"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"write"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"seek"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"resize"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"close"},{"type":"text","text":"), "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fsync"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"unlink"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FileManager"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"createDirectory"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"setAttributes"},{"type":"text","text":" (the file protection class), "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"contentsOfDirectory"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isExcludedFromBackup"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It reads no file’s timestamps, size from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"stat"},{"type":"text","text":", or the volume’s free space: a segment’s size is the offset "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"seek"},{"type":"text","text":" returns at its end, and the store bounds itself by the bytes it has written."}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FileManager.fileExists"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Data(contentsOf:)"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Data.write(to: